## What Problem This Solves

Fixes an issue where users or plugin authors writing Markdown command, hook, skill, or skill-workshop proposal files could have content starting with non-delimiter dash prefixes such as `---not` or `----` interpreted as YAML frontmatter when the file was just ordinary Markdown.

## Why This Change Was Made

The shared frontmatter parser now recognizes only full delimiter lines as frontmatter fences, after BOM and line-ending normalization. Claude bundle command prompt stripping and skill-workshop proposal extraction/stripping now use the same exact delimiter-line contract, so metadata parsing and body extraction do not drift through copied prefix checks.

## User Impact

Markdown content that starts with dash-prefixed text is preserved as body text unless it starts with a real `---` delimiter line. Valid frontmatter blocks continue to parse, and command plus workshop proposal paths no longer lose body content on the `---not` edge case.

## Evidence

